# Testing conventions

Every new feature or bugfix MUST have unit test coverage.

## Layout

- `tests/unit_tests/` — no network calls; use mocks/fixtures.
- `tests/integration_tests/` — network calls permitted; needs API keys in CI.
- Test file structure MUST mirror source code structure.

## Unit test requirements

- Use `pytest`; follow patterns in existing tests in the same package.
- Tests must be deterministic (no flaky tests).
- Cover happy path, edge cases, and error conditions.
- Use fixtures/mocks for external dependencies.

## Checklist before opening a PR

- [ ] Tests fail when the new logic is broken
- [ ] Happy path covered
- [ ] Edge cases and errors tested
- [ ] External deps mocked in unit tests
- [ ] No network calls in unit tests

## Running tests

From the package directory (e.g. `libs/partners/anthropic/`):

```bash
make test                                    # all unit tests
make test TEST_FILE=tests/unit_tests/test_x.py
make integration_tests                       # needs credentials
```
